WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:09.913
The next time Dr. Warren visited Pollyanna, he was accompanied by another doctor.

2
00:00:09.914 --> 00:00:18.635
"Dr. Chilton! I'm so glad to see you!" Pollyanna shouted happily before she remembered her aunt's opinion of him.

3
00:00:18.636 --> 00:00:23.078
"Oh, but if Aunt Polly doesn't want you—"

4
00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:28.832
"It's all right, my dear." Aunt Polly put down the book she'd been reading to Pollyanna.

5
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:34.201
"I told Dr. Warren that I wanted Dr. Chilton to examine you."

6
00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:41.568
"Oh, you asked him to come." Pollyanna smiled contentedly at this explanation.

7
00:00:41.569 --> 00:00:47.434
"Yes, dear, I asked him. That is . . ."

8
00:00:47.435 --> 00:00:56.273
Seeing the adoring look on Dr. Chilton's face, Aunt Polly turned red, sprang from her chair, and ran from the room.

9
00:00:56.274 --> 00:01:03.883
Dr. Chilton followed Aunt Polly with his eyes. "Well, Pollyanna . . ."

10
00:01:03.884 --> 00:01:08.477
He cleared his throat, but his voice was still shaking with emotion.

11
00:01:08.478 --> 00:01:13.789
"Well, Pollyanna, you've just done the gladdest thing of all!"

12
00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:19.297
"I have?" Pollyanna didn't understand what was going on.

13
00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:23.023
"Yes, you've done something to make me very glad.

14
00:01:23.024 --> 00:01:28.943
Now let's take a look at those legs."

15
00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:33.196
*** At the end of the day, Aunt Polly returned to Pollyanna's bedside.

16
00:01:33.197 --> 00:01:38.445
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you look so pretty!" Pollyanna said.

17
00:01:38.446 --> 00:01:44.078
"You look like you did when I dressed you up with the rose and shawl. What has happened?"

18
00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:51.345
Aunt Polly laughed, a joyous laugh that Pollyanna had never heard before.

19
00:01:51.346 --> 00:01:59.406
"I want you to be the first person to know—Dr. Chilton is going to be your uncle Thomas!

20
00:01:59.407 --> 00:02:07.050
We're getting married! We're both so happy, and it's all thanks to you."

21
00:02:07.051 --> 00:02:15.582
"Oh, Aunt Polly, that's wonderful news!" Pollyanna started to clap her hands but stopped.

22
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:23.590
"Wait a minute. Does that mean you were the woman whose hand and heart he wanted a long time ago?"

23
00:02:23.591 --> 00:02:33.014
Aunt Polly nodded. "We broke off our engagement after a silly argument, but you brought us together again."

24
00:02:33.015 --> 00:02:41.417
Pollyanna suddenly understood. "So that's why Dr. Chilton said I'd done the gladdest thing of all.

25
00:02:41.418 --> 00:02:47.343
I'm so glad right now that I don't even mind about my legs!"

26
00:02:47.344 --> 00:02:55.385
"Someday you might . . ." Aunt Polly didn't dare to raise Pollyanna's hopes that she might walk again.

27
00:02:55.386 --> 00:02:59.407
She smoothed Pollyanna's hair with her hand.

28
00:02:59.408 --> 00:03:04.748
"Next week you're going on a long trip to stay with a great doctor.

29
00:03:04.749 --> 00:03:11.152
He's a friend of Dr. Chilton's, and he runs a clinic just for patients like you.

30
00:03:11.153 --> 00:03:15.134
We're going to see if there's anything he can do for you."

31
00:03:15.135 --> 00:03:28.185
"Oh, Aunt Polly, if he's a friend of Dr. Chilton's, I'm sure he can help me."

32
00:03:28.186 --> 00:03:34.559
*** Many months later Aunt Polly and Uncle Thomas received a letter that made them very

33
00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.735
glad. Dear Aunt Polly and Uncle

34
00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:45.302
Thomas, I can walk! Today I walked all the way from my bed to the

35
00:03:45.303 --> 00:03:51.796
window! It was only six steps, but oh, how good it felt to walk

36
00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:55.349
again. All the doctors stood around and

37
00:03:55.350 --> 00:04:00.577
smiled. A lady who walked for the first time last week stood at my door and

38
00:04:00.578 --> 00:04:07.354
watched. Another lady, who hopes to walk next month, lay on the other bed in my room and clapped her

39
00:04:07.355 --> 00:04:13.506
hands. It was like a party except both ladies and all the nurses were

40
00:04:13.507 --> 00:04:17.432
crying. I don't understand why everybody was in

41
00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:22.252
tears. I wanted to sing and shout and bang doors!

42
00:04:22.253 --> 00:04:28.005
After walking today, I don't mind that I've been here almost ten months.

43
00:04:28.006 --> 00:04:35.069
You made sure that I didn't miss the most important event that happened during that time: your wedding!

44
00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:40.176
I still can't believe you got married right here at my bedside!

45
00:04:40.177 --> 00:04:47.968
Not only did I get to attend your wedding, but so did all the doctors and nurses and patients and staff.

46
00:04:47.969 --> 00:04:52.732
Your wedding made everybody at the clinic feel glad!

47
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:56.601
The doctors say I'll soon be going home.

48
00:04:56.602 --> 00:05:01.079
I wish I could walk all the way there.

49
00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:05.006
I don't think I'll ever want to ride anywhere again.

50
00:05:05.007 --> 00:05:12.448
(Well, maybe I'll want an occasional ride in your carriage, Uncle Thomas. I always loved that!)

51
00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:17.211
Oh, I'm so glad about everything these days.

52
00:05:17.212 --> 00:05:21.706
I'm even glad that I lost the use of my legs for a while.

53
00:05:21.707 --> 00:05:27.301
You never realize how lovely legs are until you don't have them.

54
00:05:27.302 --> 00:05:30.845
(I mean, legs that work, of course!)

55
00:05:30.846 --> 00:05:34.761
I'm going to walk eight steps tomorrow!

56
00:05:34.762 --> 00:05:38.654
With lots of love to everyone in Beldingsville,

57
00:05:38.655 --> 00:05:43.579
Pollyanna

